<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: EU pact would set fines after political steer.</title>
<headline>EU pact would set fines after political steer.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>A potential EU compromise on a budget stability pact would call for a quick decision by ministers on fines against those with big deficits, according to a draft proposal submitted to summit talks on Friday.</p>
<p>The proposal, drafted by officials for EU leaders, said that &quot;the council (of ministers) will impose&quot; sanctions on those with excessive deficits according to pre-established guidelines.</p>
<p>&quot;The resolution of the European Council...will give political direction on the means of applying this procedure in an efficient and quick way,&quot; the proposal, a copy of which was obtained by Reuters, said.</p>
</text>
